<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinderzeche</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kinderzeche is an annual historical festival in Dinkelsbühl, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, held each July. It recalls the legend that in 1632, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, the town's children persuaded a Swedish colonel to spare the town. Its name comes from an older school festival at which the children were treated, and it features a play, processions and the town's boys' band.</p></div>
